They can rain down magic missile on everything after the quest too,
and never get close to melee range.

And it's not a question of PW, really--I'd much rather not have
confuse monster at all than have it stacked up infinitely on magicbane
at no cost.  Post-quest, the only things that are a real threat are
things like purple L, titans, archons, etc that you absolutely _don't_
want confused (and potentially running out of spell lines/melee range
but still able to summon nasties).  Conflict gives you a more
consistent "monsters attack each other" benefit, plus helps burn
calories, plus doesn't cause monsters to run away randomly--keeping
them relatively predictable is a big win, especially for the real
nasties.



